.TH "OPENSTACKDOCSTHEME" "1" "Apr 03, 2026" "3.6.0" "openstackdocstheme"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
openstackdocstheme \- openstackdocstheme 3.6.0
.sp
\fIopenstackdocstheme\fP is a Sphinx documentation extension that includes
theme support for Open Infrastructure Foundation projects.
.sp
The \fIopenstackdocs\fP theme is used for documentation that is published
to docs.openstack.org and developer.openstack.org. It is intended for
use by OpenStack projects governed by the Technical Committee \%<https://\:governance\:.openstack\:.org/\:reference/\:projects/\:index\:.html>\&.
.sp
The \fIstarlingxdocs\fP theme is used for documentation that is published
to docs.starlingx.io. It is intended for use by StarlingX
projects governed by the Technical Steering Committee \%<https://\:docs\:.starlingx\:.io/\:governance/\:reference/\:projects/\:index\:.html>\&.
.SH USING THE THEME
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Prior to using this theme, ensure your project can use the OpenStack brand
by referring to the brand guidelines at \%<https://\:www\:.openstack\:.org/\:brand>\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Some of the settings below are included in the file generated by Sphinx when
you initialize a project, so they may already have values that need to be
changed.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
Update the requirements list for your project to include
\fBopenstackdocstheme\fP (usually in \fBtest\-requirements.txt\fP).
.IP 2. 3
If your project previously used the \fIoslosphinx\fP theme (without modifying
the header navigation), remove \fBoslosphinx\fP from your requirements list,
and then in your \fBconf.py\fP you can remove the import statement and
extension listing for \fIoslosphinx\fP\&.
.IP 3. 3
Once done, you should add \fB\(aqopenstackdocstheme\(aq\fP to the list of extensions
Sphinx needs to initialize and configure the theme:
.INDENT 3.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
extensions = [
    # ...
    \(aqopenstackdocstheme\(aq,
    # ...
]

html_theme = \(aqopenstackdocs\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP 4. 3
Set the options to link to the git repository on \fBhttps://opendev.org\fP and
bug tracker.
.INDENT 3.0
.TP
.B \fBopenstackdocs_repo_name\fP
The prefix and repo name. For example,
\fB\(aqopenstack/python\-glanceclient\(aq\fP\&.
.TP
.B \fBopenstackdocs_use_storyboard\fP
Set to \fBTrue\fP if using StoryBoard.
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
If using StoryBoard, do not set \fBbug_project\fP and \fBbug_tag\fP
options.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fBopenstackdocs_bug_project\fP
The project name or ID. For launchpad, it\(aqs a string like
\fBpython\-glanceclient\fP\&. If unspecified, the \(dqReport a bug\(dq
links are not shown. This option can be removed if using StoryBoard.
.TP
.B \fBopenstackdocs_bug_tag\fP
Launchpad bug tag. If unspecified, no tag is set. The default is empty.
This option can be removed if using StoryBoard.
.UNINDENT
.sp
One example for a project using launchpad:
.INDENT 3.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# openstackdocstheme options
openstackdocs_repo_name = \(aqopenstack/python\-glanceclient\(aq
openstackdocs_bug_project = \(aqpython\-glanceclient\(aq
openstackdocs_bug_tag = \(aq\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
One example for a project using StoryBoard:
.INDENT 3.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# openstackdocstheme options
openstackdocs_repo_name = \(aqopenstack/infra\-manual\(aq
openstackdocs_use_storyboard = true
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP 5. 3
Remove the options that will be automatically configured by the theme.
.INDENT 3.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBproject\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhtml_last_updated_fmt\fP
.UNINDENT
.IP 6. 3
Configure version\-related options.
.sp
For everything except documentation in the \fBapi\-guide\fP, \fBapi\-ref\fP, and
\fBreleasenotes\fP paths, the theme will automatically set the version of your
documentation. This behavior can be manually configured by setting the
\fBopenstackdocs_auto_version\fP option to either \fBTrue\fP or \fBFalse\fP\&.
.sp
If your documentation is auto\-versioned, you should remove the options
related to versioning as they will be overridden.
.INDENT 3.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBversion\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrelease\fP
.UNINDENT
.IP 7. 3
(Optional) Manually configure the project name.
.sp
The theme will automatically set the project name used in your
documentation. You can disable this behavior by setting the
\fBopenstackdocs_auto_name\fP option to \fBfalse\fP and configuring the
\fBproject\fP option to the name you wish to use.
.IP 8. 3
(Optional) Link to the PDF file.
.sp
If you build a PDF file as well, the theme can create a link to it.
Set \fBopenstack_pdf_link\fP to \fBTrue\fP to generate the link.
The file is expected to be named \fBdoc\-<shortname>.pdf\fP and placed
in the top\-level directory where \fB<shortname>\fP is the
\fBopenstackdocs_repo_name\fP\&. For example with:
.INDENT 3.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
openstackdocs_repo_name = \(dqopenstack/python\-glanceclient\(dq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
the shortname is \fBpython\-glanceclient\fP and the filename will be
\fBdoc\-python\-glanceclient.pdf\fP\&. Use the variable
\fBopenstackdocs_pdf_filename\fP to override the generated file name.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Changed in version 2.2.0: The config options \fBopenstack_pdf_link\fP and
\fBopenstackdocs_pdf_filename\fP were introduced.

.sp
Changed in version 2.1.0: The \fBrepository_name\fP, \fBbug_project\fP, \fBbug_tag\fP and \fBuse_storyboard\fP
config options were renamed to \fBopenstackdocs_repo_name\fP,
\fBopenstackdocs_bug_project\fP, \fBopenstackdocs_bug_tag\fP and
\fBopenstackdocs_use_storyboard\fP, respectively. Aliases are provided but
these will be removed in a future release.

.sp
Changed in version 2.1.0: The \fBopenstackdocs_auto_version\fP and \fBopenstackdocs_auto_name\fP config
options were added.

.sp
Changed in version 1.20: In older versions of \fIopenstackdocstheme\fP, it was necessary to manually
configure the \fBhtml_last_updated_fmt\fP option for HTML output and the
\fBlatex_engine\fP and \fBlatex_elements\fP options if you required PDF output.
This is no longer the case as these attributes are now configured
automatically.

.SH ADDITIONAL CONFIGURATION
.sp
If you are using this theme for API reference documentation, set the sidebar
navigation in the \fBhtml_theme_options\fP in the \fBconf.py\fP file:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# To use the API Reference sidebar dropdown menu,
# uncomment the html_theme_options parameter.  The theme
# variable, sidebar_dropdown, should be set to \(gaapi_ref\(ga.
# Otherwise, the list of links for the User and Ops docs
# appear in the sidebar dropdown menu.
html_theme_options = {
    # ...
    \(dqsidebar_dropdown\(dq: \(dqapi_ref\(dq,
    \(dqsidebar_mode\(dq: \(dqtoc\(dq,
    # ...
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The search bar in the sidebar is disabled by default. To enable it, set
the \fBsidebar_search\fP option to \fBTrue\fP for project\-scoped search:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
html_theme_options = {
    # ...
    \(dqsidebar_search\(dq: True,
    # ...
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If you are using this theme for documentation you want to release based on git
tags on your repository, set the release dropdown menu option in the
\fBhtml_theme_options\fP in the \fBconf.py\fP file. By default it is set to
\fBFalse\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
html_theme_options = {
    # ...
    \(dqshow_other_versions\(dq: \(dqTrue\(dq,
    # ...
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If you are using this theme for a project with published documentation that
predates the Mitaka release cycle, set the earliest published version in the
\fBhtml_theme_options\fP in the \fBconf.py\fP file to the name of the first series
with documentation available. By default it is set to \fBNone\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
html_theme_options = {
    # ...
    \(dqearliest_published_series\(dq: \(dqgrizzly\(dq,
    # ...
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBWarning:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Do not use this for release\-notes as they are always published as one
document with internal versioning.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
A badge pointing out the support status of a document is shown now
for repositories that have \fBstable/\fP branches. The badge is not
displayed for api\-ref, api\-guide and releasenotes documents. It
can be disabled with the \fBdisplay_badge\fP html theme option:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
    html_theme_options = {
    # ...
    \(dqdisplay_badge\(dq: False,
    # ...
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The TOC on the left contains a global section (to navigate between pages)
and a local section (showing page contents). If the TOC is displayed in the
text, you might want to disable the global section of the TOC:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
html_theme_options = {
    # ...
    \(dqdisplay_global_toc_section\(dq: False,
    # ...
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If you are using this theme for something other than docs.openstack.org,
you can customize the root title (\(dqOpenStack Docs\(dq) that appears in the
page title and the left arrow tooltip:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
html_theme_options = {
    # ...
    \(dqroot_title\(dq: \(dqOpenStack Governance\(dq,
    # ...
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH EXTERNAL LINK HELPER
.sp
The configuration option \fBopenstack_projects\fP can be used to define
custom roles that build links that update automatically when branches
are created for each release series. Builds on the master branch link
to the \fBlatest\fP documentation.
.sp
In the \fBconf.py\fP for the source documentation, add:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
openstack_projects = [\(aqhorizon\(aq]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then in the documentation source, link to a target using syntax like:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
:horizon\-doc:\(gaLaunching Instances with Horizon <user/launch\-instances.html>\(ga
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Do not use this feature to reference projects that have a different branching
policy, for example, only have a master branch.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH DEMONSTRATION EXAMPLE
.sp
The demo documentation provides example output to ensure it matches what\(aqs
expected. The link below points to the example output when using the theme
for all documentation that is not API reference.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 2.5
[image: Documentation Logo]
[image]
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Demo documentation
.sp
The demo documentation provides example markup for looking at the expected output.
.SS Sidebar
.sp
This is a sidebar which may be used to provide related or reference
material.  It is displayed in proximity to, but outside the main
text.
.sp
The project aims for simple implementation, massive scalability, and a rich set
of features. Cloud computing experts from around the world contribute to the project.
.SS Glossary
.sp
Here\(aqs an example glossary:
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Cactus
An OpenStack grouped release of projects that came out in the spring of
2011. It included Compute (nova), Object Storage (swift), and the Image
service (glance). Cactus is a city in Texas, US and is the code name for
the third release of OpenStack. When OpenStack releases went from three to
six months long, the code name of the release changed to match a geography
nearest the previous summit.
.TP
.B CADF
Cloud Auditing Data Federation (CADF) is a specification for audit event
data. CADF is supported by OpenStack Identity.
.TP
.B CALL
One of the RPC primitives used by the OpenStack message queue software.
Sends a message and waits for a response.
.UNINDENT
.SS Literal Blocks
.sp
Here\(aqs an example configuration:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
[DEFAULT]
\&...
my_ip = 10.0.0.31
vnc_enabled = True
vncserver_listen = 0.0.0.0
vncserver_proxyclient_address = 10.0.0.31
novncproxy_base_url = http://controller:6080/vnc_auto.html
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Code Blocks
.sp
Here\(aqs another example that\(aqs python code:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def builder_inited(app):
    theme_dir = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \(aqtheme\(aq)
    LOG.info(\(aqUsing openstack theme from %s\(aq % theme_dir)
    # Insert our theme directory at the front of the search path and
    # force the theme setting to use the one in the package. This is
    # done here, instead of in setup(), because conf.py is read after
    # setup() runs, so if the conf contains these values the user
    # values overwrite these. That\(aqs not bad for the theme, but it
    # breaks the search path.
    app.config.html_theme_path.insert(0, theme_dir)
    # Set the theme name
    app.config.html_theme = \(aqopenstack\(aq
    # Re\-initialize the builder, if it has the method for setting up
    # the templates and theme.
    if hasattr(app.builder, \(aqinit_templates\(aq):
        app.builder.init_templates()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Here\(aqs the same example but with \fB\&..code\-block: ini\fP to test the pygments
lexer:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
[DEFAULT]
\&...
my_ip = 10.0.0.31
vnc_enabled = True
vncserver_listen = 0.0.0.0
vncserver_proxyclient_address = 10.0.0.31
novncproxy_base_url = http://controller:6080/vnc_auto.html
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
